IO-27: read GHCN climate files in tenths of a degree C when no Units are given

climate_readParams() defaulted the units of a GHCN-Daily climate file to
degrees F in US models and degrees C in SI models. The input reference gives
C10 (tenths of a degree C) as the default of the optional Units token on the
[TEMPERATURE] FILE line, and SWMM 5.1 always read GHCN files that way. An
older-format file used without the token was read 10 times too warm in
degrees C or as degrees F. Default to DEG_C10, as documented and as 6.0.0
does. The same setting selects the evaporation and wind units of the file
(tenths of mm, tenths of m/s or km/day), so they follow. Files with an
explicit C or F token are unchanged.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-27_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/climate.c b/src/legacy/engine/climate.c
index c343b93..0364460 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/climate.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/climate.c
@@ -570,10 +570,8 @@ int climate_readParams(char *tok[], int ntoks)
             }
         }
 
-        // --- file temperature units
-        FileTempUnits = DEG_F;
-        if (UnitSystem == SI)
-            FileTempUnits = DEG_C;
+        // --- file temperature units (default is tenths of a degree C)
+        FileTempUnits = DEG_C10;
         if (ntoks > 3)
         {
             i = findmatch(tok[3], TempUnitsWords);
